WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:06.520
Homelander in space, a brutal Butcher murder,
and an extended Love Sausage scene are just

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:10.280
a few of The Boys Season 2's most twisted
deleted scenes.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:15.020
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm revealing the original ending

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:18.839
to the second season plus seven more deleted
scenes you never got to see!

00:00:18.839 --> 00:00:21.499
Obviously, spoilers ahead, so take care.

00:00:21.499 --> 00:00:26.270
By the end of Season 2, Homelander finds himself
defeated on numerous fronts.

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:31.650
He's lost his son Ryan to Butcher, Stormfront
has been maimed and exposed as a Nazi, and

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:35.640
he's been blackmailed by Maeve into welcoming
Starlight back into the Seven.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:41.080
So, by his final scene, he attempts to heal
his bruised ego on the New York rooftops repeating

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:43.550
to himself "I can do whatever I want".

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:48.720
However, The Boys showrunner Eric Kripke has
now revealed an alternate ending with Homelander

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:50.570
in space instead.

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:55.300
Speaking to The Wrap, Kripke said that originally
Homelander was "hovering over the earth, […] like

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:59.010
Superman does, but [he] had [...] a scary
sociopathic look."

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:03.590
According to Kripke, the scene was actually
filmed and was "awesome", but Amazon asked

00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:06.820
"if [they] could stick the landing on [Homelander]
a little harder.

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:10.369
And […] have something that maybe [wasn't]
quite as ambiguous."

00:01:10.369 --> 00:01:15.270
So, Kripke decided to go back to a Season
1 deleted scene of Homelander on the Chrysler

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:19.369
Building which interestingly Amazon had refused
to allow at the time,

00:01:19.369 --> 00:01:22.260
and he submitted that as the new Season 2
ending.

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:25.439
Amazon preferred this recycled finale because,
as Kripke says,

00:01:25.439 --> 00:01:29.780
"it's telling us something about how powerless
and pathetic [Homelander] feels in that moment

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:32.770
and how dangerous he'll be moving into Season
3."

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:37.749
I can see why they opted to change the ending,
but personally I think a really menacing scene

00:01:37.749 --> 00:01:43.130
of Homelander in space looking down on Earth
would have been more interesting as it'd look

00:01:43.130 --> 00:01:45.490
like he's threatening the whole world.

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:49.240
And it would have tied in stronger with the
idea that's been building in Season 2 that

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:52.630
Homelander could go completely off the rails
at any point.

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:56.960
For example, there was the moment where he
imagined himself massacring the crowd who

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:59.659
were booing him,
and there was the threat he made to Maeve

00:01:59.659 --> 00:02:03.189
in the final episode if she released the video
of the airplane incident.

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:04.840
"If you do that..

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:07.740
..I'll destroy everything
and everyone."

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:12.470
After A-Train is ejected from the Seven, he
becomes desperate to get back in the team,

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:16.980
and there's a great deleted scene which sheds
a lot more light on his motivations to return

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:18.099
to the spotlight.

00:02:18.099 --> 00:02:22.879
In the cut scene, A-Train visits his financial
adviser to discover that despite the fact

00:02:22.879 --> 00:02:27.900
that he earns over 40 million a year, he has
less than a quarter of a million left.

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:29.080
"240 thousand dollars.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:31.450
Nah, this.. this can't be right.

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:33.030
Run those numbers again."

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:35.099
"I have trust me, that's all you got."

00:02:35.099 --> 00:02:38.099
"I make 40 million dollars a year."

00:02:38.099 --> 00:02:43.420
The adviser goes on to list all the deductions
taken out of A-Train's income such as..

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:44.420
"..taxes.

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:47.640
There's also commissions from your agents,
your managers, your lawyers, me.

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:52.010
You've got two dozen people on your payroll,
and that's not counting friends and relatives."

00:02:52.010 --> 00:02:57.019
And after A-Train tries to justify this by
claiming he has responsibilities, his adviser

00:02:57.019 --> 00:02:59.700
notes all the speedster's crazy expenditures.

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:06.560
"13 houses, a private jet, an island that
you've never been to, and paying to have Jan

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:08.890
Michael Vincent's ashes shot into space.

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:13.180
And then he drops the even bigger bombshell
that A-Train doesn't even have the rights

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:14.709
to exploit his own brand.

00:03:14.709 --> 00:03:16.800
"Get booted from the Seven, so f-ing what?

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:17.800
I still got this.

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:18.800
I'm still A-Train."

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:22.000
"Actually bruh, you're not.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:26.900
You see, Vought owns the name, the uniform,
everything."

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:31.209
Basically, Vought can completely destroy him
financially if he attempts to use the name

00:03:31.209 --> 00:03:32.870
in any commercial endeavour.

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:33.870
"I'm A-Train!

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:40.060
If I wanna open up A-Train's Cadillac or whatever
the f- I wanna do, that's exactly what I'm

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:41.060
gonna do."

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:43.209
"Not if you wanna get sued and lose all of
your money."

00:03:43.209 --> 00:03:47.540
This is a really interesting scene that gives
some insight into exactly how much money Supes

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:50.280
can earn if they make it to the top tier of
talent,

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:54.099
and how ill-equipped they can be to deal with
the business side of their work, like many

00:03:54.099 --> 00:03:57.640
other celebrities,
but it also shows just how expendable they

00:03:57.640 --> 00:03:59.629
are if they fall out of favour.

00:03:59.629 --> 00:04:04.049
Love Sausage is one of the – shall we say
– more intriguing Supes that the gang discover

00:04:04.049 --> 00:04:08.019
when they break into Vought's secret psych
ward in the sixth episode.

00:04:08.019 --> 00:04:12.540
And after the patients take over the asylum,
Mother's Milk suddenly finds himself attacked

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:16.799
by the Russian man's super-powered appendage
which begins to strangle him.

00:04:16.799 --> 00:04:21.440
M.M. manages to remove the monstrous thing
after Kimiko knocks Love Sausage out with

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:25.530
her brass knuckles and it recedes back into
the unconscious Supe's pants.

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:29.460
As crazy as this scene is already, originally
it was going to be even crazier.

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:34.370
In an interview with TV Line, Tomer Capon
who plays Frenchie, revealed that Laz Alonso,

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:38.650
who plays Mother's Milk, had pitched an idea
to the episode's director that during the

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:41.449
fight,
while the giant genitalia was wrapped around

00:04:41.449 --> 00:04:45.750
his neck, Frenchie should save him by biting
the prosthetic member off.

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:51.490
Capon agreed and the scene was filmed, however,
apparently the tentacle ended up torn to shreds

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:53.710
and the footage wasn't good enough to use.

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:57.970
And because only one prosthetic had been made,
they couldn't repeat the scene.

00:04:57.970 --> 00:05:02.371
According to The Boys showrunner, Love Sausage's
massive appendage was a combination of a 10-foot

00:05:02.371 --> 00:05:07.340
long animatronic puppet with extra CG effects
added in post-production.

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:11.010
Leave a thumbs-up if you like this deleted
scene and maybe one day the footage will get

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:12.540
released on a blooper reel!

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:16.949
There's a great Kimiko deleted scene from
the fourth episode where we get to see more

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:22.289
of how she tries to manage the emotional fall-out
from her brother's death at the hands of Stormfront.

00:05:22.289 --> 00:05:27.190
It starts with her watching one of the secret
Nazi's rants on social media, but then she's

00:05:27.190 --> 00:05:30.090
distracted by a rodent that's wandered into
her room.

00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:33.710
She befriends the little creature by feeding
it some snacks, and then she hears the news

00:05:33.710 --> 00:05:35.650
about Stormfront's upcoming protest.

00:05:35.650 --> 00:05:38.380
[Stormfront] "Let's show Vought what they
have to do.

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:40.510
Tomorrow morning, Vought Square.

00:05:40.510 --> 00:05:42.090
Be your own hero.

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:43.240
Do not let me down."

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:48.080
The scene fades and we find Kimiko pacing
nervously until she discovers the friendly

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:51.260
creature has died in a trap underneath her
bed.

00:05:51.260 --> 00:05:55.480
The animal's death is particularly upsetting
because it reminds her of her murdered brother

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:58.690
Kenji, and the nickname "mouse" that she used
to call him.

00:05:58.690 --> 00:06:03.389
If it looked like Kimiko was in two minds
over whether to confront Stormfront at the

00:06:03.389 --> 00:06:08.229
rally, it seems like the rodent's death was
what ultimately led her to that decision.

00:06:08.229 --> 00:06:10.910
"Kimiko, open the door please.

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:12.390
Kimiko!"

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:18.479
There's an interesting deleted scene from
the first episode in which we see Frenchie

00:06:18.479 --> 00:06:21.910
argue with Cherie over the special relationship
he has with Kimiko.

00:06:21.910 --> 00:06:23.590
"Okay, it's not like that, okay!"

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:25.389
"You wanna f- her, f- her.

00:06:25.389 --> 00:06:26.480
Just spread the wealth."

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:27.480
"We are not..

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:28.590
..I would never sleep with her."

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:30.300
"Oh yeah, then what is she to you then?

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:32.730
I mean, I see the way you look at her."

00:06:32.730 --> 00:06:35.300
"It's difficult, it's difficult to explain,
she's special."

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:38.020
Cherie doesn't buy what Frenchie is saying
and mocks him.

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:42.000
"So me, you can pull me by the hair and f-
me sideways, but her..

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:43.900
..she's too magic and special, huh?"

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:48.520
This scene helps to better set up the moment
later in Season 2 when Frenchie attempts to

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:49.930
kiss Kimiko.

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:53.669
Plus it adds more weight to the scene where
he confesses to Cherie that he tried it on

00:06:53.669 --> 00:06:54.669
with her.

00:06:54.669 --> 00:06:57.300
"You thought a kiss would make her feel better
or you feel better?"

00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:01.979
When Billy Butcher turned up at the very end
of the Season 2 premiere, we didn't get any

00:07:01.979 --> 00:07:06.521
proper explanation of where he'd been in between
the Season 1 finale and reuniting with the

00:07:06.521 --> 00:07:08.440
Boys this season.

00:07:08.440 --> 00:07:11.940
Originally a lengthy five-minute scene was
going to fill in the gaps, but it ended up

00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:15.550
cut and released instead as a short film titled
"Butcher".

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:20.650
The original scene reveals that after Butcher
left Tony Cicero's, he steals a car and drives

00:07:20.650 --> 00:07:23.710
to the house of an old SAS friend called Jock.

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:27.090
After reminiscing for a while about their
days in the field, Butcher asks Jock if he

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:28.690
can help him find his wife Becca.

00:07:28.690 --> 00:07:31.400
"Thought maybe you could put some feelers
out you know?

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:33.750
Get some of the old intel boys, Higgins, Esquerra."

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:35.670
"All respect, yeah?

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:37.729
Doesn't seem to me like your girl wants to
be found."

00:07:37.729 --> 00:07:41.840
"Look, are you going to f-ing help me or not?"

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:44.710
"Course I am, we're mates, aren't we?"

00:07:44.710 --> 00:07:48.319
After re-emerging from the shower wearing
the tracksuit that Frenchie asked him about

00:07:48.319 --> 00:07:52.480
in the first episode, Butcher discovers that
Jock has sold him out and called the authorities.

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:53.480
"Ordering pizza are we?"

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:54.480
"Take it easy mate.

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:56.599
Plodders are on their way."

00:07:56.599 --> 00:07:58.210
"You shouldn't have done that Jock."

00:07:58.210 --> 00:07:59.930
"You topped that Stillwell woman on the telly.

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:03.289
You gonna top your wife as well?"

00:08:03.289 --> 00:08:05.120
"I didn't kill no one."

00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:08.690
"Come on Billy, I seen what you can do.

00:08:08.690 --> 00:08:09.780
You're a killer down to the ground.

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:10.780
That don't change."

00:08:10.780 --> 00:08:14.319
The two fight, and Butcher, proving his friend
right in a way, chokes him to death and torches

00:08:14.319 --> 00:08:15.360
the whole house.

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:19.600
I can see why this didn't make it into the
show because it's a side story that isn't

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:24.800
that crucial for the main plot and would have
slowed down an early episode had it been included.

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:29.620
It does show Butcher, as we've seen a few
other times, at his most ruthless and murderous.

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:34.050
Clearly his friend was betraying him without
asking Butcher whether any of the news stories

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:37.110
were really true,
but Butcher certainly didn't hold back on

00:08:37.110 --> 00:08:40.750
finishing the guy off, when he could have
just incapacitated him.

00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:45.640
There's a curious deleted scene from the third
episode with Stormfront and Maeve reacting

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:49.940
to the news leaks about Vought secretly administering
Compound V to babies.

00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:51.270
"Did you know about this?"

00:08:51.270 --> 00:08:52.270
"No.

00:08:52.270 --> 00:08:53.950
But I mean are you really surprised?

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:58.100
Some a- stood up in a meeting and said we
could make a race of super-beings that we

00:08:58.100 --> 00:09:01.490
can control, own and monetize.

00:09:01.490 --> 00:09:04.710
All we have to do is inject a few babies."

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:08.940
It's a shame this scene was cut because it
helps give more reasons as to why Queen Maeve

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:12.760
changed her mind about helping Starlight in
the final episode.

00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:17.140
When Maeve watched Stormfront stride past
her in the Tower as the details of her Nazi

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:20.490
past broke on the news,
she doubtless would have remembered the pretence

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:24.870
Stormfront made of not knowing anything about
Compound V in this deleted scene.

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:28.860
One of Stormfront's secrets is that she was
the first person who was successfully injected

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:33.200
with Compound V by her Nazi husband Frederick
Vought, something she was more than happy

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:34.649
to disclose to Homelander.

00:09:34.649 --> 00:09:39.550
We know Mother's Milk is all about his family
and as a way of trying to keep himself in

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:42.500
balance while trapped in the Boys' underground
hideaway,

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:47.350
throughout the second season we see him constructing
a large dollhouse which he plans to give to

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:48.640
his daughter Janine.

00:09:48.640 --> 00:09:52.700
And a scene cut from episode 4 would have
revealed what happened when he finally finished

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:53.700
it.

00:09:53.700 --> 00:09:58.490
In the deleted scene, we see M.M. meticulously
dust and finish off the grand dollhouse,

00:09:58.490 --> 00:10:04.209
but as he contemplates his achievement he
decides instead to offer it to someone else:

00:10:04.209 --> 00:10:05.209
"Hey.

00:10:05.209 --> 00:10:07.529
You got a little girl, don't you?"

00:10:07.529 --> 00:10:08.779
"8 years old."

00:10:08.779 --> 00:10:10.029
"Give her this.

00:10:10.029 --> 00:10:11.279
It's all yours."

00:10:11.279 --> 00:10:14.610
This would have been a nice character moment
for Mother's Milk as it shows him accepting

00:10:14.610 --> 00:10:18.220
the reality of the situation that he can't
be with his family right now.

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:22.460
So, do you wish any of these deleted scenes
had been included in Season 2?

00:10:22.460 --> 00:10:25.610
And would you have preferred the original
ending of Homelander in space?

00:10:25.610 --> 00:10:27.600
Leave your thoughts in the comments below.

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:31.990
And if you enjoyed any of these scenes, a
thumbs-up is hugely appreciated.

00:10:31.990 --> 00:10:36.440
Next tap left to check out my full deleted
scenes and alternate endings playlist or tap

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:38.260
right for something else you're sure to like.

00:10:38.260 --> 00:10:40.430
Thanks for watching and see ya next time.

00:10:40.430 --> 00:10:41.750
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

